  "limitations": [
    "Checked input is still MOL2 only. Output is MOL2, SMILES or CJSON; checked CJSON input/self-conversion is not supported.",
    "Strict MOL2 → CJSON refuses because source metadata and partial charges are lost and source chemical interpretation remains unverified.",
    "CJSON coordinates are marked preserved only with verified projected-graph correspondence and exact f64 bits; source decimal spelling and physical dimensionality are outside this check.",
    "Projected formal charges are not independent validation of source formal-charge semantics. Only the N.4 rule is interpreted; geometry/extension stereo and source hydrogen assignment remain unverified.",
    "Zero/query bond projection changes yield unverified graph/mapping, not a preservation claim. CJSON does not apply the recursive SMILES 512-atom cap but still enforces reader and output limits.",
    "30 parity cases (23 identical reports, 7 shared errors) and seeded finite precision vectors are exposed development regressions, not an independent chemistry or Open Babel acceptance corpus.",
    "Enabling the serde_json dependency feature affects shared numeric JSON parsing in dependent builds. No performance comparison was made.",
